Reform UK leader Nigel Farage says he believes Prime Minister Keir Starmer "doesn't have a plan" to tackle the migrant crisis and instead "hopes it will all go away".

"It's simply about fairness, people are incensed! Young males get everything free."

@Nigel_Farage

“There is a huge problem with how we’re approaching the division between economic migration and genuine asylum.”

Keir Starmer says he will review Italy's asylum deal with Albania as part of a "pragmatic" approach to addressing Channel migrant crossings.

@iancollinsuk | #Talk

Low-skilled migrant workers cost taxpayers more than £150,000 each by the time they reach state pension age.

Broadcaster and commentator Rafe Heydel-Mankoo: "The British people have been betrayed and lied to for years."

@Iromg | @RafHM

